From: sbe1v1k 25.12-6.12 port <noreply@sbe1v1k-build>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: ipq95xx: declare Spectrum SBE1V1K LAN/WAN ports

Without a spectrum,sbe1v1k case, board.d/02_network falls through to
"Unsupported hardware" and package/base-files' 99-default_network
writes lan=eth0 / wan=eth1.  That is both incomplete (two of the four
ports) and wrong: on this board eth1 (dp2, QCA8081 2.5G, PPE port 5)
is the WAN port and eth0 (dp1, RTL8261N 10G, PPE port 6), eth2 and
eth3 are the LAN ports (see patches/0011).  This is the port layout the
24.10-6.6 tree established on hardware and the vendor board.d
matches.

eth0 is listed in the LAN set so board.json advertises it and LuCI's
port panel shows all four ports, but netifd must not own it: applying
a LAN address change makes netifd tear the port down and the RTL8261N
falls into a fake 10G loopback.  The uci-defaults script
99-spectrum-eth0-unmanaged-lan (files overlay) strips it back out of
the generated br-lan, and /usr/sbin/eth0-lan-attach re-adds it as a
bridge member from outside netifd.  Same arrangement as 24.10.

Port roles (2026-11-21, stage A of docs/WAN_LAN_ROLE_SWITCH): the
WAN assignment is no longer hardcoded.  sbe_ports.main.wan_port is
read from UCI and selects eth0 (10G) or eth1 (2.5G) as WAN, or none
(all four ports in LAN).  Unset or invalid values keep the original
behaviour (eth1 WAN), so factory reset and upgrade paths are
unchanged.  This branch only runs when /etc/board.json does not
exist; runtime role changes are handled by /usr/sbin/sbe-port-roles
(init S19), which also rewrites the board.json network section.

LuCI builds the status -> overview port panel from the board.json
network section (luci-mod-status 29_ports.js): it reads lan.ports[]
and wan.device, so the fallback leaves two ports showing with the
roles reversed.  ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan() emits a
space-separated LAN list as a "ports" array, which is exactly the
shape 29_ports.js expects.

Status: static only, NOT TESTED on hardware.
---
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
@@ -17,6 +17,27 @@
 	qcom,ipq9574-ap-al02-c7)
 		ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan "lan1 lan2 lan3 lan4 lan5" "wan"
 		;;
+	spectrum,sbe1v1k)
+		# 端口角色（2026-11-21 阶段 A）：sbe_ports.main.wan_port 决定
+		# eth0/eth1 谁是 WAN；未设置或非法值回落今天的场景 3（eth1 WAN）。
+		# 本脚本只在 board.json 不存在时运行；运行期切换由 sbe-port-roles
+		# 重建 board.json 网络段，不依赖这里。
+		local wan_port
+		wan_port=$(uci -q get sbe_ports.main.wan_port 2>/dev/null)
+		case "$wan_port" in
+		eth0)
+			# 场景 1：eth0（10G）作 WAN；eth1 回到 br-lan。
+			ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan "eth1 eth2 eth3" "eth0"
+			;;
+		none)
+			# 场景 2：没有 WAN；四个口都在 LAN（eth0 仍由 helper 挂桥）。
+			ucidef_set_interface_lan "eth1 eth2 eth3 eth0"
+			;;
+		*)
+			ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan "eth2 eth3 eth0" "eth1"
+			;;
+		esac
+		;;
 	*)
 		echo "Unsupported hardware. Network interfaces not initialized"
 		;;
